<div id="2026-10-11-private-print-upload" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-10-11 — Public hub counts and private print upload</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> <code>/3d</code> shows the public-model count to everyone. The full library count is an admin-only card. Browse has an upload that creates a private model (owner tag, never public), reads STL volume for a filament estimate, and queues a print. The farm slices before a printer starts.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> The public hub was showing the whole library. Customers need to bring a file found on a model search, or one they made, without publishing it.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Controller/3d.pm</code>, <code>Controller/3d/PrintUpload.pm</code>, <code>root/3d/index.tt</code>, <code>root/3d/browse.tt</code></p>
</div>
